.TH CLANG-INSTALLAPI 1 "" "LLVM @LLVM_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clang-installapi \- generate and verify Apple text-based library interfaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clang-installapi
.BI \-target " apple-target"
.BI \-install_name " library-name"
.BI \-o " output.tbd"
.RI [ options ] " " "header-list.json | framework-directory"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Parse library headers with Clang and write a text-based stub library describing
its exported interface. Inputs are JSON header lists or a framework directory.
The selected target must be an Apple platform supported by TextAPI; this command
does not produce Peios ELF shared libraries.
.PP
A target SDK, headers and framework search paths must be supplied when required
by the input. The output path is mandatory. Multiple input header lists can be
combined. If several input directories are given, the last directory is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-target " triple"
Select an Apple target triple, including the deployment version. May be repeated
for multiple slices. Do not combine with \-arch or \-mtargetos.
.TP
.BI \-o " path"
Write the interface to this file; a dash selects standard output.
.TP
.BI \-install_name " name"
Set the dynamic library install name recorded in the interface.
.TP
.BI \-isysroot " directory"
Use this SDK root while parsing headers.
.TP
.BI \-I " directory"
Add a header search directory. Clang framework, language and preprocessing
options can also be supplied, including \-F, \-x, \-D and \-U.
.TP
.BI \-\-filetype= " format"
Select tbd-v4 or tbd-v5 output.
.TP
.BI \-verify-against " library"
Compare the generated interface with an existing dynamic library or framework.
.TP
.BI \-\-verify-mode= " mode"
Select ErrorsOnly, ErrorsAndWarnings or Pedantic verification.
.TP
.B \-\-demangle
Demangle symbols in diagnostics.
.TP
.BI \-extra-public-header " path"
Add a public header. The corresponding \-extra-private-header and
\-extra-project-header options select private or project headers.
.TP
.BI \-exclude-public-header " glob"
Exclude public headers matching a pattern. Corresponding private and project
options are also available. Quote patterns to prevent shell expansion.
.TP
.BI \-public-umbrella-header " path"
Select the public umbrella header. Private and project variants are available.
.TP
.BI \-reexport_library " path"
Re-export another library. The \-reexport-l and \-reexport_framework options
accept a library name or framework name respectively.
.TP
.BI \-allowable_client " name"
Restrict clients allowed to link against the library.
.SH INPUT FORMAT
A version 3 header list has a version field and a headers array. Each header
entry specifies a type, such as public or private, and its path. For example:
.nf
{ "version": "3", "headers": [
  { "type": "public", "path": "include/example.h" }
] }
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful interface generation. A nonzero status indicates an
invalid invocation, an input or output error, or a failed verification.
.SH NOTES
This command's upstream driver does not implement a standalone help response.
This reference describes the packaged driver's option table and input parser.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clang (1),
.BR llvm-readtapi (1)
